# QUANDA-AI-MODELS.SKILLS — AI Model & Agentic Capability Extension
Version: 1.0
Source snapshot: DMS4 Client Solutions — Models tab, 2026B screenshots supplied by user
Purpose: Extend QUANDA's ontology with contemporary hosted and open/open-weight AI model families so the V2 solver can reason about model choice as one possible execution tool.
Scope note: AI model names, limits, access routes, licensing, and provider positioning change quickly. Treat the entries below as a dated course snapshot, not timeless truth. Verify current provider documentation before production deployment, purchasing, licensing, or client-facing claims.
Integration note: This file is designed to sit beside `knowledge/quanda.skills` and be compiled into the same runtime ontology. Do not overwrite the stable base ontology when model metadata changes.
Selection note: QUANDA should recommend a model only when the project actually benefits from AI assistance. "Use AI" is not a default production step.
Decision note: Model selection should be based on project fit, access, cost, privacy, deployment constraints, modality, context needs, tool use, user familiarity, and verification requirements — not benchmark rank alone.

## 1. AI Model Provider / Family Index

### Proprietary / Hosted API families
- OpenAI
- Claude / Anthropic
- Gemini / Google
- Grok / xAI

### Open / Open-weight families
- Llama / Meta
- DeepSeek
- Kimi / Moonshot AI
- Qwen / Alibaba
- Gemma / Google DeepMind
- GLM / Zhipu AI / Z.ai

