### OpenAI GPT-5.5
- canonical_id: ai-model.openai.gpt-5-5
- family: GPT
- provider: OpenAI
- provider_type: proprietary
- access:
  - hosted API
  - ChatGPT ecosystem
  - Codex ecosystem
- license: proprietary API
- context_window_snapshot: 1,048,576 tokens
- max_output_snapshot: up to 128,000 tokens
- model_roles:
  - frontier hosted reasoning model
  - senior coding collaborator
  - agentic coding model
  - long-context project reviewer
  - structured-output model
  - tool-using model
- strong_for:
  - complex full-stack builds requiring careful edits across multiple files
  - repository-scale reasoning
  - tool-heavy agent workflows
  - debugging
  - technical architecture
  - UI critique
  - reasoning-heavy product decisions
  - long-context review of project folders
  - briefs
  - user research
  - assessment evidence
- useful_execution_methods:
  - delegate_to_agent
  - code_generation
  - code_review
  - repository_analysis
  - structured_extraction
  - planning
  - debugging
- typical_uses:
  - primary implementation partner in Codex or compatible coding agents
  - turn research or survey findings into prioritized implementation tasks
  - produce structured JSON, issue lists, test plans, and deployment checklists
  - use lower reasoning effort for routine edits and higher effort for architecture, difficult bugs, or final verification
- watch_for:
  - paid hosted usage
  - token cost
  - data handling
  - quota limits
  - higher pricing for unusually large prompts
  - capable output still requires human review and testing
- best_role_summary: primary senior coding collaborator for complex implementation, review, and tool-heavy project work
- volatility: high
- freshness_policy: verify provider docs before production use

