## 4. QUANDA V2 Model-Selection Factors

### Hard Filters
- project explicitly forbids hosted AI
- project explicitly requires local inference
- project explicitly requires a named provider or model
- user has no API access for a required hosted route
- model cannot support the required modality
- model cannot fit required context / file size after realistic chunking strategy
- required tool-calling or structured-output support is unavailable
- license terms conflict with intended deployment
- data-handling constraints conflict with provider route
- available hardware cannot run the selected local model
- deployment runtime cannot support the selected model
- budget constraint makes route infeasible

### Primary Ranking Signals
- task fit
- user access
- user familiarity
- coding quality fit
- agentic/tool-use fit
- multimodal fit
- context requirement
- latency requirement
- cost fit
- privacy fit
- local-vs-hosted preference
- deployment compatibility
- structured-output reliability
- language fit
- resource / documentation quality
- current model availability

### Secondary Ranking Signals
- provider ecosystem fit
- existing project integrations
- benchmark evidence
- community adoption
- local runtime convenience
- hardware efficiency
- portability
- model personality / prose style
- novelty

### Strong Penalties
- switching to a new provider with no project-specific benefit
- requiring a paid API when a known free/local route satisfies the task
- recommending a huge local model to a laptop-only user
- recommending a preview alias for an important deployment without version pinning
- using a reasoning-heavy model for trivial copy edits
- using a general chat model when deterministic code would solve the task better
- using any model when no AI assistance is necessary

## 5. Model Selection by Project Need

### Need: Repository-Level Agentic Coding
- prefer candidates:
  - OpenAI GPT-5.5
  - Claude Opus 4.8
  - GLM-5
  - Kimi K2.6
  - DeepSeek coding variants
  - Qwen coding variants
- evaluate:
  - repository access
  - tool permissions
  - test execution
  - code-edit reliability
  - context size
  - user review ability
  - cost

### Need: Multimodal Project Understanding
- prefer candidates:
  - Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview
  - OpenAI GPT multimodal family
  - Claude multimodal family
  - Llama 4
  - Gemma 4
- evaluate:
  - screenshot / image support
  - document support
  - structured output
  - privacy
  - file-size limits
  - cost

### Need: Local / Offline Prototype
- prefer candidates:
  - Qwen3
  - Gemma 4
  - Llama 4
  - GLM-5
  - DeepSeek open checkpoints
  - Kimi open checkpoints
- evaluate:
  - RAM
  - VRAM
  - quantization
  - model size
  - inference runtime
  - latency
  - license
  - battery / thermal constraints

### Need: Low-Cost Reasoning
- prefer candidates:
  - DeepSeek family
  - Qwen family
  - smaller Gemma variants
  - suitable GLM variants
- compare against:
  - paid frontier APIs
- verify:
  - current endpoint price
  - current free tier
  - context limits
  - quality on the project's actual task

### Need: Google-Centric Workflow
- prefer candidates:
  - Gemini
  - Gemma where local/open deployment is desired
- relevant integrations:
  - Google AI Studio
  - Gemini API
  - Google Cloud
  - Firebase
  - Google Drive
  - Google Docs

### Need: Provider Comparison / Research
- candidate set:
  - OpenAI
  - Claude
  - Gemini
  - Grok
  - DeepSeek
  - Qwen
  - Llama
  - Gemma
  - Kimi
  - GLM
- compare with:
  - same prompt
  - same task
  - same rubric
  - same validation data
- measure:
  - task success
  - latency
  - cost
  - tool-use reliability
  - code quality
  - structured-output validity
  - hallucination rate
  - human correction time

